# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# Every real route is emitted as its own dist/<route>/index.html at build time, and dist/404.html
# makes Pages return a genuine 404 for anything else (it previously served index.html with a 200 —
# a soft 404 that Lighthouse caught via the llms.txt audit).
#
# /auth/* is the one route that cannot be a static file: it is a wildcard that forwards emailed
# verify/reset links to the beta app, so the path is not known ahead of time. This rewrite (200,
# not a redirect) hands those to the SPA shell. It is scoped to /auth/ only, so it cannot shadow
# any prerendered page.
/auth/*  /index.html  200
